  "question": {
    "text": "Consider the following reaction\n\\(\\mathrm{MnO}_2+\\mathrm{KOH}+\\mathrm{O}_2 \\rightarrow \\mathrm{A}+\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}\\).\nProduct ' \\(\\mathrm{A}\\) ' in neutral or acidic medium disproportionate to give products ' \\(\\mathrm{B}\\) ' and ' \\(\\mathrm{C}\\) ' along with water. The sum of spin-only magnetic moment values of \\(\\mathrm{B}\\) and \\(\\mathrm{C}\\) is \\(\\qquad\\) BM. (nearest integer) (Given atomic number of \\(\\mathrm{Mn}\\) is 25)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{MnO}_2+\\mathrm{KOH}+\\mathrm{O}_2 \\rightarrow \\mathrm{K}_2 \\mathrm{MnO}_4+\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}$\n(A)\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{K}_2 \\mathrm{MnO}_4 \\xrightarrow{\\text { Neutral/acidic solution }} \\mathrm{KMnO}_4+\\mathrm{MnO}_2 \\\\\n& \\mathrm{Mn}^{+4}:-[\\mathrm{Ar}] 3 \\mathrm{~d}^3 \\\\\n& \\mathrm{n}=3, \\mu=\\sqrt{3(3+2)}=3.87 \\text { B.M. }\n\\end{aligned}$<br />Nearest integer is (4)",
    "image": null
  },
